Bandicot was my first attempt at a gnomish healer. He found an early
magic lamp, which provided a tame djinni. Spending time near his large
dog and the djinni sped his descent to minetown, where he bought
protection and found three bones files, including one with Frost
Brand, Magicbane,  "oR, Cloak of MR, a magic marker, a =oSD, a
luckstone, and many spellbooks. Handing Frost Brand to the djinni
resulted in the death of everything in the minetown level, excepting
Izchak. He converted the alter, blessed the waters, wrote some
blessed ?oI and ID everything he was holding. After un-cursing the
good stuff, he  dove to mines-end, where his large dog found a poly-
trap and became [larger] black dragon.

Proceeding to Sokoban, he found another magic lamp, which he stashed
pending completion of sokoban. Sokoban went smoothly, except that his
pet D fell through to a level below and lost his tameness. The zoo
closet contained another amulet, so he blessed his magic lamp an
wished for a bBOH.

Bandicot trekked back to minetown, where he put something in his BOH
that caused it to explode. I had my wand of cancellation in my main
inventory; (I think the offending object was a cursed bag of tricks.
Bags of holding were identified, as were wands of cancellation. I
thought that cursed sack was safe because I'd previously looted it
without being bitten; maybe it had no charges?). Stupid, stupid
mistake. Lost most everything, but he was still well equipped in his
main inventory (and non-burdened), so he dove deep into the mines. (My
only previous ascension also included a blown BoH, so I judged this
unfortunate event to be a temporary setback.) Alas, things continued
to get worse (though bandicot remained optimistic). He angered a
storekeeper and killed him in self defense ('You murderer!"). Shortly
thereafter, he angered his djinni with a bounced spell and had to
dispatch him. Nevertheless, he continued to dive to Medusa's level.

Entering the level, he noted a purple worm near the stairs. He
resolved to jump (using his discovered jumping boots) around the worm,
exploring the dry area near the stairs. He hadn't planned on a
sleeping trap. This led to a cruel loop of falling asleep, being
engulfed, being regurgitated directly onto the trap, falling asleep
again. After a few dozen loops: DYWYPI?

This was a particularly frustrating death, because bandicot's kit was
shaping up so nicely: MR and reflection, two great artifact weapons,
casting sleep at 0% fail, jump boots, and slow digestion. I was
looking forward to whacking the cyclops and taking his toy. At this
point, I just wish I'd eaten more elves.

